`./doc/wiiland.7`, `./doc/libxwiimote.7`, `./doc/wiilandd.1`,
`./doc/wiiland-config.1`, and `./doc/xwiishow.1`: installed manpages

`./doc/DEVICES` and `./doc/DEV_*`: device enumeration and protocol descriptions

Copying
=======

See `./COPYING` for licensing and authorship information.

Compatibility
=============

Two other commonly used Wii-Remote libraries are cwiid and wiiuse. Both
provide a full user-space driver and were used heavily in the past. WiiLand
does not provide API compatibility with them:

* cwiid is highly asynchronous and thread-oriented, which does not permit a
  single-threaded application to use the API naturally.
* wiiuse is tightly bound to application-managed Bluetooth discovery and
  connection, static remote arrays, and callbacks; its API is substantially
  different from WiiLand's.

The WiiLand API has few restrictions and can support event-based,
callback-based, thread-based, or other event loops. It remains close to the
kernel API so applications can integrate it into their existing
infrastructure.

WiiLand is forked from xwiimote by David Herrmann. See `./COPYING` for
authorship and contributor credits.

